From: Anton Argirov <anton.argirov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tsconf): prioritize SD reads over Kempston mouse

TSConf decodes SD data port 57h by its low byte. INIR changes the high byte,
which can match the generic partial Kempston mouse decoder and corrupt SD
reads when mouse emulation is enabled. Read TSConf SD data before the mouse.

---
diff --git a/src/operaciones.c b/src/operaciones.c
--- a/src/operaciones.c
+++ b/src/operaciones.c
@@ -7326,6 +7326,9 @@
     }
 
 
+	/* TSConf SD uses an 8-bit port decode. INIR changes B and must not
+	   route SD data reads through the partially decoded Kempston mouse. */
+	if (MACHINE_IS_TSCONF && puerto_l==0x57) return tsconf_sd_read_byte();
 
 	/* BaseConf decodifica #xxDF y usa A10/A8 para distinguir botones, X e Y.
 	   Las demás máquinas conservan la decodificación parcial genérica. */
@@ -7905,13 +7908,8 @@
 
         if (puerto_l==0x77) {
             return zcontroller_enabled.v ? 0 : 1;
-        }
-
-        if (puerto_l==0x57) {
-            return tsconf_sd_read_byte();
         }
 
-
 	}
 
 
